    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "22. **Staging:**\n\n- **Manual Sign-Off:** Update requests should be validated by stakeholders to confirm alignment with business objectives and no unintended consequences.\n\n- **Security & Compliance Checks:** Using automated tools to scan for vulnerabilities and ensure compliance with financial regulations can prevent reputational damage.\n\n- **Load Testing:** Simultaneously spinning up production-like traffic and tasks to verify system performance, capacity, and resilience under stress.\n\n23. **Production:**\n\n- **Monitoring and Alerting:** Deploy feature flags and monitor application performance in real-time. Set up alerts for any anomalies and ensure a rapid response team is on standby.\n\n- **Rollback Procedures:** Have clear and tested rollback procedures in place in case new features result in critical issues after deployment.\n\n- **Health Checks:** Take pre-deployment snapshots and establish baseline health indicators such as latency, response times, and error rates. Automate comparison tests against these baselines post-deployment to detect deviations.\n\n28. **Post-Deployment:**\n\n- **A/B Testing:** Gradually shift traffic from the old version to the new version to gauge impact and collect user feedback before full-scale rollout.\n\n- **Data Integrity Validation:** Compare pre and post-deployment application performance metrics and user experience indicators such as transaction success",
